### BuildWithAspire MCP Server (HTTP Transport)
### Remote MCP Server with HTTP-based tool execution
### Base URL: Auto-assigned port (check Aspire dashboard)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:38717

### === Server Status and Health ===

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Server Status (shows transport type and available tools)
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### === MCP Tool Discovery ===

### List All Available Tools
GET {{baseUrl}}/tools

### === Weather Tools ===

### Get Current Weather
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetCurrentWeather
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Get Weather Forecast (5 days default)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetWeatherForecast
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "MaxDays": 5
}

### Get Weather Forecast (custom days)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetWeatherForecast
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "MaxDays": 3
}

### Get Weather Forecast (maximum 10 days)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetWeatherForecast
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "MaxDays": 10
}

### Convert Temperature (Celsius to Fahrenheit)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/ConvertTemperature
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Temperature": 25.0,
  "FromUnit": "C"
}

### Convert Temperature (Fahrenheit to Celsius)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/ConvertTemperature
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Temperature": 77.0,
  "FromUnit": "F"
}

### === System Tools ===

### Get Current Date and Time
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetCurrentDateTime
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Get System Information
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GetSystemInfo
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Generate Random Number (default range 1-100)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GenerateRandomNumber
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Min": 1,
  "Max": 100
}

### Generate Random Number (custom range)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GenerateRandomNumber
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Min": 10,
  "Max": 50
}

### === Encoding Tools ===

### Encode Text to Base64
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/EncodeToBase64
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Hello, MCP World!"
}

### Decode Base64 to Text
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/DecodeFromBase64
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "base64Text": "SGVsbG8sIE1DUCBXb3JsZCE="
}

### === Math Tools ===

### Basic Addition
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "A": 15.5,
  "B": 7.3,
  "Operation": "add"
}

### Basic Multiplication
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "A": 12,
  "B": 8,
  "Operation": "multiply"
}

### Division
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "A": 100,
  "B": 4,
  "Operation": "divide"
}

### Square Root
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/SquareRoot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": 64
}

### Power Calculation
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Power
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "baseNumber": 2,
  "exponent": 8
}

### Generate Fibonacci Sequence
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/GenerateFibonacci
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "terms": 10
}

### Check if Number is Prime
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/IsPrime
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": 97
}

### Check if Number is Prime (not prime)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/IsPrime
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": 100
}

### === Tool Testing Examples ===

### Test Complex Math Chain
### 1. Calculate: (5 + 3) = 8
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "A": 5,
  "B": 3,
  "Operation": "add"
}

### 2. Power: 8^2 = 64
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Power
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "baseNumber": 8,
  "exponent": 2
}

### 3. Square Root: √64 = 8
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/SquareRoot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": 64
}

### 4. Check if 8 is Prime (no)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/IsPrime
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": 8
}

### === Error Testing ===

### Test Invalid Tool Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/NonExistentTool
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Test Division by Zero
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/Calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "A": 10,
  "B": 0,
  "Operation": "divide"
}

### Test Negative Square Root
POST {{baseUrl}}/tools/SquareRoot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": -25
}